  "displayField": "",
  "description": "&lt;div style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&amp;quot;Avenir Next&amp;quot;, Avenir, &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:inherit; font-size:large;\"&gt;&lt;font style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is this data?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&amp;quot;Avenir Next&amp;quot;, Avenir, &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&amp;quot;Avenir Next&amp;quot;, Avenir, &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; margin:0px 0px 1rem 0in; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:inherit;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;This feature layer depicts land use within northeastern Illinois broken out into 57 categories. Parcels were dissolved on common land use types, and polygons were generated for non-parcel areas (e.g. road rights-of-way) and assigned a generic \u201cnon-parcel\u201d category.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&amp;quot;Avenir Next&amp;quot;, Avenir, &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\"&gt;&lt;div style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;div style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:inherit; font-size:large;\"&gt;&lt;font style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How can it be used? What projects use this data?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:inherit;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;Land Use data can be used for forecasting, land use and transportation modeling, existing conditions reports and general research.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:inherit; font-size:large;\"&gt;&lt;font style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who created this data? How and when?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:inherit; font-size:medium;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;Data was created by CMAP staff, updating the previous 2020 inventory using Spring 2023 aerial photography as the base, supplemented by County Assessor files and other data.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:inherit; font-size:large;\"&gt;&lt;font style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where can I find the latest data?&amp;nbsp;How frequently is it updated?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:inherit; font-size:medium;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;\"&gt;Land Use Inventory files are considered final upon publication. New Land Use Inventories are produced every 3 to 5 years. They may be updated as necessary to correct data flaws, and the original files replaced.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;",
